1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:04,102
Aphrodite loved another:
Ares, the god of war.

2
00:00:04,102 --> 00:00:07,637
He was Hera's other son —
Hephaestus's own brother — the

3
00:00:07,637 --> 00:00:12,043
swiftest god on Olympus, and
the one Zeus said he hated most.

4
00:00:12,043 --> 00:00:16,385
Once, two giants had chained him in
a bronze jar for thirteen months,

5
00:00:16,385 --> 00:00:18,610
until Hermes stole him out.

6
00:00:18,610 --> 00:00:20,750
But the Sun sees everything.

7
00:00:20,869 --> 00:00:24,826
Helios saw the two of them together,
and went straight to Hephaestus.

8
00:00:24,826 --> 00:00:26,781
Hephaestus went to his forge.

9
00:00:26,781 --> 00:00:30,491
He hammered out chains as
fine as spider webs — too fine

10
00:00:30,491 --> 00:00:34,542
for any god to see, too
strong for any god to break.

11
00:00:34,542 --> 00:00:38,076
He fixed them around his bed, and
hung them from the roof beams.

12
00:00:38,135 --> 00:00:41,062
Then he announced that he
was leaving for Lemnos.

13
00:00:41,096 --> 00:00:43,156
Ares had been watching the house.

14
00:00:43,163 --> 00:00:44,530
He came at once.

15
00:00:44,530 --> 00:00:47,979
The two lay down together — and
the chains closed around them,

16
00:00:47,979 --> 00:00:50,119
and neither could lift a limb.
